Z||000007||tgowens||07-25-2001||12:06 PM||||The factory sub will work with the factory set up as well as an aftermarket set up. It is all in the way you wire it......<P><BR>fierovette, first check to see that all of the components are there - overhead switch, wiring harness that runs from the switch down the a-pillar to the junction block on the top of the left body shroud (you can see this by removing the left speaker), the wiring harness to the sub amp, the sub amp (located behind the carpet and the console support against the console on the passenger side), and the sub woofer speaker and enclosure (located under the dash on the right side on the passenger side). If all of those components are there, check to make sure they are all connected properly. It is possible that the speaker is blown and not emitting sound. My guess is that there is a plug unplugged somewhere.......<P><p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 07-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fierochic88||07-25-2001||01:10 PM||||I just got done installing a factory sub this weekend and I already have Kenwoods and I did notice a difference.<P>Jennifer||||reg||1
